      },
      "reasoning_reference": "tests/reference/reasoning_baseline.py",
      "reasoning_local_changes": "Grading runs in a time-limited worker process (TimeLimitedGrader); timeouts and grader exceptions score 0 and are recorded. Rollouts sample on the model's device from an explicit, checkpointed generator. grpo_step backpropagates each rollout separately (same gradient as the source's mean loss) and, when all rewards are equal, sets zero gradients without the forward/backward pass. Training is float32 with SDPA attention; the source holds embedding and linear weights and their AdamW state in bfloat16 (RMSNorm scales float32). MATH data is pinned by commit URL and SHA-256.",
      "distill_reference": "tests/reference/instruction_baseline.py (build_examples, filter_examples_by_max_len, compute_example_loss)",
      "distill_local_changes": "Prompt-masked targets (-100) replace slicing logits at prompt_len - 1; tested equal in loss and gradient. Batches come from a seeded DataLoader shuffle instead of random.Random(seed); validation loss is token-weighted over the 25 examples."
